  "id": "Compound::DB00257 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Clotrimazole exhibits a consistent interaction with Cyp2c8 through a series of mechanistic pathways. The drug binds to Cyp3a7, which then participates in aromatase activity, ultimately leading to Cyp2c8 being involved in the metabolism of xenobiotics. This suggests that Clotrimazole may inhibit Cyp2c8 through a pathway involving Cyp3a7 and aromatase. Additionally, Clotrimazole also binds to Cyp19a1, which participates in aromatase activity, further reinforcing the involvement of Cyp2c8 in the metabolic processes of xenobiotics. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Clotrimazole influences Cyp2c8, although the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Clotrimazole and Cyp2c8, mediated through the shared participation in aromatase activity and the involvement of Cyp3a7.",
